      "width": 560,
      "height": 460,
      "data": {
        "view": {
          "intent": "node",
          "payload": "node.web.detail"
        },
        "interfaceContract": {
          "version": 1,
          "ownsContent": true
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Custom Event + Bridge Smoke — Receiver\n\nConsumes the `widget.ready` custom Event declared (and raised) by `qa/custom-event-bridge-smoke/source`'s Widget Ready (Event Source) Method.\n\n## Import from Source\n\nAn import Bridge pointed at the source graph. Open its Events section (BridgeEventsPanel.js) to see `widget.ready` listed as exposed, and the Handler below assigned to it.\n\n## Remote Trigger Demo\n\nAn Event Handler -- not a Method -- because a bridged trigger has no single node in this graph to point an edge at. Its Action Method port is wired to Remote Action.\n\nA direct Method `trigger` edge (like the source graph's Local Trigger Demo) only works for Events declared in the *same* graph; see MethodTriggersEditor.js and the plan doc's \"what's still data, not a port\" note for why.\n\nAutomated coverage for this same scenario: `tests/customEventBridgeSmoke.test.js` in the twilite repo."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "receiver-declaration",
          "nodeId": "receiver-overview"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "receiver-glyph",
      "type": "glyph",
      "label": "Glyph",
      "position": {
        "x": -800,
        "y": 120
      },
      "width": 220,
      "height": 140,
      "data": {
        "glyph": {
          "kind": "icon",
          "name": "Bolt"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "receiver-declaration",
          "nodeId": "receiver-glyph"
        }
      }
    },
    {
